     "text": "[{\"text\": \"No anomalies were detected by flow cytometry\", \"excluded\": true}, {\"text\": \"Cytogenetic studies showed a normal diploid karyotype\", \"excluded\": true}, {\"text\": \"no abnormalities were identified by a myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS)/MPN fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) panel\", \"excluded\": true}, {\"text\": \"JAK2 p.V617F mutation analysis by next-generation sequencing (NGS) and BCR/ABL1 qualitative screening by reverse transcriptase polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR) were unremarkable\", \"excluded\": true}, {\"text\": \"Other established driver mutations in genes that are associated with various MPNs, including those in JAK2 (exons 12\u201315), TPO receptor (MPL), and calreticulin (CALR) were not detected\", \"excluded\": true}, {\"text\": \"Flow cytometry was unremarkable\", \"excluded\": true}, {\"text\": \"Cytogenetic studies by karyotype analysis and a FISH panel for MDS/MPN showed normal results including proves for JAK2, PDGFRA, PDGFRB, and FGFR1 gene rearrangements\", \"excluded\": true}, {\"text\": \"Screening for Fanconi anemia by chromosome breakage using mitomycin C or diepoxybutane was unremarkable\", \"excluded\": true}]"
